<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sretenje Constitution</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1835</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Candlemas Constitution, Constitution of the Principality of Serbia (1835)</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sretenje Constitution was the first constitution of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a>, adopted at Kragujevac on 15 February 1835, the feast of Sretenje (Candlemas). Drawn up to limit the autocratic rule of Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milos-obrenovic">Miloš Obrenović</a>, it divided power between the prince, a state council and an assembly and abolished feudal obligations. Under pressure from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> it was suspended within weeks.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sretenje-constitution.jpg" alt="Sretenje Constitution" width="320" height="450" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dimitrije Davidović and Stefan Radichević. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Constitution_of_1835.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
